{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCaptured nested pytest sessions that do not receive a private --basetemp join pytest's user-global numbered temporary root and may delete unrelated cleanup-eligible trees at session finish. The parent pytest process owns the temporary lifetime, so each nested child must use a unique basetemp under its parent's tmp_path. This bug was discovered from grindable-deviant-angwantibo after its runtime RCA confirmed the cleanup mechanism.\n\n## Complete nested-pytest inventory\n- tests/_store_isolation.py:32-48 is safe: it passes tmp_path / nested-pytest as --basetemp.\n- tests/unit/test_external_isolation.py:62-78 is safe: it passes tmp_path / bt as --basetemp.\n- tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py:13-31 is safe: it passes tmp_path / nested-basetemp as --basetemp.\n- tests/unit/test_git_version_floor.py:143-178 is unsafe: its real nested collection has no --basetemp.\n- tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:826-848 is unsafe: its shared real-collection helper has no --basetemp.\n- tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py:148-204 is unsafe: its mixed-module nested run has no --basetemp.\n- tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py:142-178 is unsafe: its standalone bare-pytest run has no --basetemp.\n- tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py:82-116 is unsafe: its parametrized bare-pytest collection has no --basetemp.\n\nThe literal pytest occurrences in tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py:134 and tests/unit/grounding/test_deps.py:286-298 are test data, not subprocess launch sites. A repository-wide AST scan of calls containing the pytest literal plus a literal-string search for console-script construction found no other live nested launch sites.\n\n## Approach\nThread each outer test's parent-owned tmp_path into its nested launch and pass a distinct child path through --basetemp. For the shared collection helper, make the basetemp an explicit Path argument supplied by each calling test. This follows the already-green ownership pattern in tests/_store_isolation.py:32-48 and tests/unit/test_external_isolation.py:62-78, keeps cleanup local to the parent fixture, and preserves each child's interpreter or console-script entrypoint, cwd, selectors, marker expressions, plugins, and assertions.\n\nAdd a behavior-level real-subprocess regression. The outer subprocess receives its own --basetemp, while PYTEST_DEBUG_TEMPROOT points at an isolated shared numbered root containing a byte sentinel old enough for pytest cleanup. Each affected outer test is driven through its real nested launch; the sentinel must remain present with identical bytes. This crosses the actual pytest cleanup seam without timing sleeps or source-text assertions.\n\n## Scope\n- tests/unit/test_git_version_floor.py: parent-owned basetemp for the under-floor collection child.\n- tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py: explicit parent-owned basetemp through the real-collection helper and both callers.\n- tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py: parent-owned basetemp for the mixed-module child.\n- tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py: parent-owned basetemp for the standalone bare-pytest child.\n- tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py: parent-owned basetemp for each parametrized bare-pytest child.\n- tests/unit/test_nested_pytest_basetemp.py: real-subprocess regression over every repaired launch site.\n\nNo production module, dependency, configuration key, or public API changes.\n\n## Testing\n- RED oracle: under an isolated PYTEST_DEBUG_TEMPROOT, create several numbered pytest roots so the oldest sentinel is cleanup-eligible; run each affected outer test with an outer --basetemp; assert exact sentinel bytes remain.\n- Contrast/control: the driven outer tests must still return success, proving their existing entrypoint, cwd, selection, marker, and assertion contracts remain intact.\n- Mutation: remove one repaired --basetemp pair to restore the exact defect and confirm the corresponding behavior-level case returns RED, then restore it.\n- Focused: run the new regression and all five affected modules.\n- Broad: run the default unit selection used by CI, then make lint and make typecheck.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every live nested pytest subprocess has a unique parent-owned --basetemp; verified by the complete inventory above and the behavior-level parametrized regression in tests/unit/test_nested_pytest_basetemp.py.\n- [ ] Each affected real nested launch leaves a cleanup-eligible shared numbered-tree sentinel byte-for-byte unchanged; verified by pytest -q tests/unit/test_nested_pytest_basetemp.py.\n- [ ] The existing entrypoint, cwd, selector, marker, plugin, and child-assertion contracts for all five repaired modules remain green; verified by focused execution of those modules.\n- [ ] The exact-defect mutation removing a repaired --basetemp makes its held-out behavior case fail, and restoring the repair makes it pass.\n- [ ] The CI default unit selection, make lint, and make typecheck all exit zero.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787026487251037001,"uuid":"d6e57940-3198-48f2-b892-b1b5739459a3"}